# What must never enter the build context.
#
# The Dockerfile is `COPY . .`, so anything not excluded here is baked into the
# image, and an image is not a secret: anyone who can pull it or run
# `docker save` can read every layer.
#
# The previous version of this file listed `.env` alone. Docker matches that
# literally, so `.env.dev` - DB_PASSWORD and REFRESH_TOKEN_SECRET - was copied
# in, and so was `certs/private.pem`, the RSA key that signs every access token.
# A container built from any developer's working tree therefore ran on that
# developer's signing key, and anyone holding the image could mint an access
# token for any user.
#
# It also defeated the CMD. `[ -f certs/private.pem ] || npm run keys:generate`
# is meant to give each deployment its own key pair; with the key already in the
# image the guard was satisfied and generation never ran.

# Secrets and per-environment configuration.
certs/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local state that is nobody else's business and bloats the context.
logs/
.postgres/
node_modules
coverage
build
.git
.github
.husky

# Noise.
npm-debug.log
*.log
